Simplest fix: Split evidence into per-item files under common-sense-evidence/ directory. Keep the tracker as a 3KB summary index. This would save ~1.5MB/day.

Alternative (even simpler): Modify your common-sense-verify workflow to read common-sense-status.md first to pick the target item, then use offset/limit to read only that item's row from the full tracker. Avoids file restructuring.","heartbeatTriggered":false,"requestId":"42f9a903"}

